# Generated data files must never be line-merged.
# Git's 3-way merge will happily interleave two versions of a JSON array or CSV
# and produce a file that is still syntactically valid but has the wrong number
# of rows — silent corruption that no test catches. This happened once when the
# scheduled refresh landed mid-push. Marking them binary forces an explicit
# conflict instead, and the correct resolution is always to re-run the fetcher.
data/*.json -merge -diff
data/*.csv  -merge -diff
